ight be just list. Safer to output JSON with fields.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P2383\nimplementability_evidence: ...\nimplementability: 3\netc.\n\nProvide one sentence evidence each.\n\nMake sure evidence is one sentence.\n\nImplementability evidence: Creating a dedicated real-time interface for logging matches and verifier identities requires new software development but uses existing logging infrastructure, making it reasonably feasible. -> that's one sentence.\n\nAcceptability evidence: Capturing verifier identities as mandated by Article 12(3)(d) aligns with legal requirements and does not violate norms. -> 4\n\nEffectiveness evidence: The module directly records the period of use, reference database, input matches, and verifier identity required by Article 12(3), thereby solving the logging mandate for Annex III systems. -> 4\n\nApplicability evidence: The proposal addresses the stated problem of meeting the EU AI Act logging mandate for high-risk R&D labs. -> 4\n\nparadigm_relatedness evidence: It introduces a new specialized tool but continues to treat compliance as separate logging practice rather than integrating it into R&D. -> 2\n\noriginality evidence: Building a dedicated traceability interface for mandated logs is a common, mundane compliance response. ->1\n\nEnsure scores correct.\n\nMaybe acceptability =4 common strategies that violate no norms. Yes.\n\nImplementability maybe 3? Could be 4 easy to implement at low cost? \"some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\" vs \"easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\". Dedicated interface might be more than non-radical. I'll keep 3.\n\nReturn.\n\n",
