ng. Seems reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability? If implemented, it would automate logging. Maybe 4.\n\nApplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 = solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Do middleware to get automatic logging -> directly related. So 4.\n\nNovelty originality (1-4):\nIdea is standardized library wrapper for logging. Is that not expressed before? Probably common. Originality: common, mundane, boring =1 ? Could be interesting? Unified telemetry middleware is fairly standard practice. Maybe interesting =2? Let's think reference class: experienced evaluator expects AI R&D labs to give responses to mandate. Middleware for logging is common suggestion. Not ingenious. Might be interesting but not unusual. Probably 2 = interesting. Or 1 = common, mundane. I think it's common practice to build wrapper for logging. Could be 2? Hmm.\n\nparadigm_relatedness (1-4):\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way unchanged\n\nUnified middleware is tool for logging, still treats compliance as logging practice. Introduces new elements (tools). So slightly paradigm stretching =2.\n\nWorkability acceptability (1-4):\n4 = common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities\nIdea is software library for logging, acceptable. 4.\n\nimplementability (1-4):\n4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 = significant change...\nDevelop lightweight wrapper around existing model inference engines integrated into all high-risk AI projects. That's some changes, reasonably feasible? Might be significant change across projects. Probably 3 = some changes, reasonably feasible. Could be 4 easy? Building standardized library may be non-radical but integrating into all projects is effort. I'd say 3.\n\nLet's output.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence one sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nOrder listed: effectiveness, applicability, originality, paradigm_relatedness, acceptability, implementability\n\nProvide evidence sentence then score.\n\nMake sure one sentence each.\n\nReturn rating.\n\nProbably JSON? Not specified. Probably list.\n\nWe'll output id P2471 then lines.\n\nLet's produce clear output.\n\n",
