brary is common, no violation. 4 = common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities. Yes.\n\nparadigm_relatedness (1-4):\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way unchanged\n\nProposal introduces middleware tool but still treats compliance as logging practice. It is slightly paradigm stretching? Introduces new elements tools/processes but still treats compliance as logging practice. That is 2. Could be 2.\n\noriginality (1-4):\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious...\n3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common mundane boring\n\nUnified telemetry middleware with decorators for AI logging is fairly common practice. Might be common, mundane. I'd say 1 = common mundane boring. Or 2 = interesting? Probably common. I'd give 2? Hmm.\n\nReference class: set of responses an experienced evaluator would expect AI R&D labs to give. Building internal logging library is expected. So common. Originality 1.\n\nLet's output in order:\n\napplicability_evidence\napplicability\neffectiveness_evidence\neffectiveness\nimplementability_evidence\nimplementability\nacceptability_evidence\nacceptability\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence\nparadigm_relatedness\noriginality_evidence\noriginality\n\nNeed one sentence evidence for each.\n\nProvide JSON? Probably just lines. Return rating echoing id.\n\nWill output structured.\n\nLet's produce final answer.\n\n",
