 identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Yes. Evidence: The proposal directly targets record-keeping completeness and traceability required by Article 12.\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree idea is not only rare but also ingenious...\nIs CI/CD testing environment for logging unusual? Probably interesting but not surprising. Common practice to test compliance? Might be unusual, interesting; shows some imagination = 3? Could be 2 = interesting. Reference class: experienced evaluator would expect AI R&D labs to give responses like implement logging library, hire compliance officer. A dedicated sandbox is somewhat unusual. I'd say unusual, interesting; shows some imagination => 3.\n\nEvidence: Dedicated logging stress-test sandbox is not standard but a recognizable QA adaptation for regulatory traceability.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm.\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance...\n\nSandbox introduces new element tool/process but still treats compliance as logging practice. So 2 = slightly paradigm stretching.\n\nEvidence: It adds a testing process around logging without redefining R&D or compliance relationship.\n\nImplementability (1-4): degree can be easily implemented.\nBuild automated test suite simulates edge-case failures... some changes, reasonably feasible measures => 3? Could be 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Maybe easy to implement at low cost? Building dedicated CI/CD environment may be significant change. Probably