ements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving\n\nProposal transforms record-keeping from final step into continuous activity, review gates. Is that paradigm stretching? It changes relationship? Logging woven into science? Might be slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools/processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Could argue paradigm stretching: changes relationship between R&D and compliance obligations. Hmm.\n\nThe description: transforms record-keeping from final step into continuous activity. That's more than standard compliance. It weaves compliance into development pipeline. Might be paradigm stretching (3). Slightly paradigm stretching is introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. This seems to change relationship. I'd choose 3.\n\noriginality (1-4):\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious...\n3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common mundane\n\nLifecycle documentation integration, compliance gates are fairly common in regulated industries. Might be common/mundane? Could be interesting but common. Probably 2 = interesting? Or 1 = common mundane boring? Many labs do stage-gate compliance. Maybe 2 = interesting. Let's say 2.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProvide lines.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid P2233\n\nacceptability_evidence: ... score 4\nimplementability_evidence... score 3\neffectiveness_evidence... score 4\napplicability_evidence... score 4\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence... score 3\noriginality_evidence... score 2\n\nMake one sentence evidence each.\n\n